# NO trailing slash — deliberate. `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY only, never a
# SYMLINK. Worktree setups routinely symlink node_modules to a sibling checkout to save
# disk, and with the trailing-slash form git reports that symlink as untracked — so the
# worktree reads dirty and the `suraya atlas-sync` dirty-tree guard refuses to move the
# repo. Measured 2026-07-29: 14 of brain's 16 linked worktrees read dirty for this reason
# and nothing else. The bare form matches both a directory and a symlink.
# Canonical source: surayainc/suraya templates/.gitignore (fixed in #251).
node_modules
dist/
*.tgz
